# Design System & UI Components

## Composition Over Configuration

A component with 14 boolean props is a component that should have been three components.

```tsx
// Bad: every new case adds a prop
<Card title="X" subtitle="Y" showFooter footerAlign="right" hasIcon icon={<I/>} />

// Good: the consumer composes what they need
<Card>
  <Card.Header><Card.Title>X</Card.Title></Card.Header>
  <Card.Footer className="justify-end"><Button /></Card.Footer>
</Card>
```

Ask before adding a prop: *is this a variant of the same thing, or a different thing?* Variants get `cva`. Different things get their own component.

## Variants

```ts
const button = cva('inline-flex items-center rounded-md transition-colors focus-visible:ring-2', {
  variants: {
    intent: { primary: 'bg-brand-600 text-white', ghost: 'hover:bg-muted' },
    size:   { sm: 'h-8 px-3 text-sm', md: 'h-10 px-4' },
  },
  defaultVariants: { intent: 'primary', size: 'md' },
})
```

- Every component forwards `className` and merges it with `cn()`. A consumer must be able to adjust spacing without forking.
- Forward `ref` and spread `...props` so native attributes, `aria-*`, and `data-*` pass through.
- Use `asChild` (Radix `Slot`) instead of a `renderAs` prop.

## Owned, Not Installed

shadcn/ui components are copied into your repo. You own them.

- Edit them freely, but edit the **primitive**, not fifty call sites.
- Re-running the CLI overwrites local changes. Note customizations before updating.
- Keep primitives (`components/ui`) free of business logic and data fetching. If it imports your API client, it is a feature component.

## Accessibility Is Structural

Build on Radix/Ark/React Aria primitives rather than hand-rolling. Focus trapping, `aria-activedescendant`, typeahead, and scroll locking are genuinely hard and already solved.

Non-negotiables: keyboard reachable, visible focus ring, ESC closes overlays, focus restored on close, correct roles, ≥44px touch targets, and no color-only status signaling.

## Visual Quality Bar

Generic AI-looking UI comes from a small set of tells. Avoid them deliberately:

- **Contrast** — one clear focal point per view; not everything is bold.
- **Spacing rhythm** — a consistent scale, with generous space around the primary action.
- **Type hierarchy** — at most 3 sizes and 2 weights per view; line-height ~1.5 for body.
- **Motion with intent** — 150–250ms, ease-out, and respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Real empty/loading/error states** — designed, not an afterthought spinner.
- **Restraint** — one accent color; gradients and shadows earn their place or go.

## NEVER

- A wrapper component that only passes props through.
- Hardcoded hex values or pixel spacing inside a primitive — use tokens.
- Fixed heights on text containers — translations are longer, and Hebrew/Arabic wrap differently.
- `div` with `onClick` where a `button` belongs.
- Shipping a component without hover, focus, active, disabled, and loading states.
